public JsonNode getRefSchemaNode(String ref) {
    JsonSchema schema = findSchemaResourceRoot();
    JsonNode node = schema.getSchemaNode();
    String jsonPointer = ref;
    if ((schema.getId() != null) && ref.startsWith(schema.getId())) {
        String refValue = ref.substring(schema.getId().length());
        jsonPointer = refValue;
    }
    if (jsonPointer.startsWith("#/")) {
        jsonPointer = jsonPointer.substring(1);
    }
    if (jsonPointer.startsWith("/")) {
        try {
            jsonPointer = URLDecoder.decode(jsonPointer, "utf-8");
        } catch (UnsupportedEncodingException e) {
            // ignored
        }
        node = node.at(jsonPointer);
        if (node.isMissingNode()) {
            node = handleNullNode(ref, schema);
        }
    }
    return node;
}
```

Branches:

1. First if: schema.getId()!=null && ref starts with schema.getId(). Cases: true and false.

2. Second if: jsonPointer starts with "#/". Cases: true and false.

3. Third if: jsonPointer starts with "/". Cases: true and false.

Inside third if: try-catch (unsupported encoding not likely) but we can simulate exception? URLDecoder.decode can throw UnsupportedEncodingException only if charset not supported; "utf-8" is supported, so not thrown. Could mock to throw? But method catches and ignores. We could simulate by using a spy to make URLDecoder.decode throw? Not easy. Might just note that exception path is covered by default.

Inside after node = node.at(jsonPointer); then if node.isMissingNode() true leads to handleNullNode call. So need case where node missing.

Thus test cases:

- Case A: schema.getId() null, ref does not start with id, jsonPointer not start with "#/", not start with "/", return original schema node.

- Case B: schema.getId() non-null, ref starts with id, after stripping, jsonPointer maybe "#/something" etc.

